8455|a|Of or pertaining to Rome, or the Roman people; like or characteristic of Rome, the Roman people, or things done by Romans; as, Roman fortitude; a Roman aqueduct; Roman art. ; Of or pertaining to the Roman Catholic religion; professing that religion. ; Upright; erect; -- said of the letters or kind of type ordinarily used, as distinguished from Italic characters. ; Expressed in letters, not in figures, as I., IV., i., iv., etc.; -- said of numerals, as distinguished from the Arabic numerals, 1, 4, etc.	j:3fjt,142,3;5l6b,134,44;5h4c,129,41;6hut,129,3920;6iee,129,40;74eo,128,11;ab8f,126,54;7011,124,24;79gw,123,23;79gv,122,167;2uq8,122,515;78j0,121,18;5v83,121,100;211q,118,36;56kp,118,25~6hut,129,3920;2uru,105,2284;2uq7,102,1063;1blz,105,645;2uq8,122,515;1blp,78,514;1ick,65,475;555n,44,469;j0w,76,428;6hno,26,425;1bls,109,424;9nyp,21,412;8txx,84,393;57c0,48,348;as9,66,256	e:2e3f,46,2;6drr,39,5;92vn,30,7;54pg,2,51;2q9v,1,16~54pg,2,51;2q9v,1,16;92vn,30,7;6drr,39,5;2e3f,46,2
