8458|n|A species of fictitious writing, originally composed in meter in the Romance dialects, and afterward in prose, such as the tales of the court of Arthur, and of Amadis of Gaul; hence, any fictitious and wonderful tale; a sort of novel, especially one which treats of surprising adventures usually befalling a hero or a heroine; a tale of extravagant adventures, of love, and the like. ; An adventure, or series of extraordinary events, resembling those narrated in romances; as, his courtship, or his life, was a romance. ; A dreamy, imaginative habit of mind; a disposition to ignore what is real; as, a girl full of romance. ; The languages, or rather the several dialects, which were originally forms of popular or vulgar Latin, and have now developed into Italian. Spanish, French, etc. (called the Romanic languages). ; A short lyric tale set to music; a song or short instrumental piece in ballad style; a romanza.	a:496d,131,56;1ha9,128,6;3z5f,120,8;r58,115,20;9tof,114,9;6w6z,108,17;8mwk,99,5;1530,97,9;jsk,95,3;9gjs,92,22;5opn,90,3;3t5k,85,12;ab5s,81,9;34ho,78,8;aiin,78,103~6r1c,38,1009;5wuf,71,403;5z2v,26,169;5js4,22,138;aiin,78,103;a9gu,39,70;496d,131,56;8k4w,24,47;qne,23,44;5i9m,37,36;43ys,52,33;7vjn,15,29;363p,68,28;2qge,67,25;5ovx,74,24	v:1530,88,5;8mwk,86,2;2lj4,75,12;6vj3,52,1;8y4i,43,9;8wp0,27,9;55zg,19,14;5bdg,17,4;2drx,16,5;4epj,10,13;an75,9,15;7r3f,3,32~7r3f,3,32;an75,9,15;55zg,19,14;4epj,10,13;2lj4,75,12;8y4i,43,9;8wp0,27,9;1530,88,5;2drx,16,5;5bdg,17,4;8mwk,86,2;6vj3,52,1	V:53nj,71,1;kh7,67,2;53py,67,289;9mkx,62,1;1myx,60,1;26sj,58,9;2eqe,49,4;9qb7,46,1;1okk,40,1;9mos,28,8;2vso,24,11;6fll,24,2;4m8m,23,5;4m8h,20,8;8wpi,11,4~53py,67,289;2vso,24,11;26sj,58,9;9mos,28,8;4m8h,20,8;4m8m,23,5;8wpi,11,4;2eqe,49,4;6fll,24,2;kh7,67,2;53nj,71,1;9mkx,62,1;9qb7,46,1;1okk,40,1;1myx,60,1	n:4ky0,118,5;1n0t,114,10;7uk2,112,8;8mwk,104,7;8c2j,101,3;3z5f,90,1;6vj3,80,7;aj6z,79,3;7jjj,73,5;r58,72,1;9gju,71,5;aifv,70,5;82ps,70,2;954,69,20;2mz5,69,10~11a,3,98;w46,11,66;by0,35,3