85h3|n|A contrivance or arrangement serving as a fulcrum for an oar in rowing. It consists sometimes of a notch in the gunwale of a boat, sometimes of a pair of pins between which the oar rests on the edge of the gunwale, sometimes of a single pin passing through the oar, or of a metal fork or stirrup pivoted in the gunwale and suporting the oar.	v:a7cv,14,3;a7g2,10,23;4a5,10,3;a6d9,7,24;3ei7,5,1;44j,2,5~a6d9,7,24;a7g2,10,23;44j,2,5;4a5,10,3;a7cv,14,3;3ei7,5,1	V:5cs9,55,3;43qq,33,1~5cs9,55,3;43qq,33,1	n:85h3,123,4;a574,111,2;43qq,43,2;43qa,39,5~43qa,39,5;85h3,123,4;a574,111,2;43qq,43,2	N:aoxh,125,2;85h3,123,4;9dbm,117,3;43qa,78,75;43qq,76,20;9d1e,1,3~43qa,78,75;43qq,76,20;85h3,123,4;9d1e,1,3;9dbm,117,3;aoxh,125,2
